# Enhance agent instructions: tell Enhance what to improve — Show & Tell
#
# Feature: on an agent's Edit page, Enhance no longer fires the moment you click
# it. It opens a modal where you choose what to improve, then shows the current
# and the enhanced instructions side by side with a short list of
# recommendations:
#   Step 1  "What to improve?" (after Refine: "Refine") — three chips, multi-
#           select: Age restriction, Competitor mentions, Clearer goal — and a
#           free-text note. Chips, text, both or neither; Enhance is always on.
#   Result  left: current instructions (read-only); right: enhanced instructions;
#           Recommendations: at most 3 one-sentence, single-line items (hidden
#           when there are none: absent on the walk, present on both results
#           of the first take — so never narrate them as a sure thing).
#           Buttons: Try again, I like it, Refine.
# This flow shows the unified agent: chips + a custom note, refine, accept.
#
# Author it with:  "author a demo from input/enhance-agent-instructions.flow"
#
# ---- measured on the walk (test agent, draft) ---------------------------------
# * A DRAFT agent's row opens its editor directly (/chatbot/{agentId}/config);
#   there is no Edit button. Open it with `open /chatbot/{agentId}/config`
#   (agentId is a target secret from SALESMSG_DEMO_AGENT_ID in .env).
# * Enhance opens the modal instantly; nothing generates until step 1's Enhance.
#   Scope that button: [aria-label="DefaultModal_Card"] [aria-label="ButtonEnhance"]
#   — the page has its own ButtonEnhance underneath.
# * Generation took ~7 s (first) and ~9 s (refine). "Try again" and "I like it"
#   are on screen WHILE it loads; ButtonRefine appears only when it is done, so
#   wait for [aria-label="ButtonRefine"].
# * The enhanced text is the 2nd [aria-label="Scrollbar_View"] in the modal;
#   the additions are far down, so hover it and scroll to show them.
# * Chips expose no selected-state attribute; check the text result instead.
# * The note placeholder reads "e.g., Add a rule for handling refund requests";
#   the driver selects all before typing, so the refine note replaces the first.
# * After "I like it": modal gone, [aria-label="TextInput_MessageField"] holds
#   the new text, [aria-label="ButtonSaveChanges"] is enabled. Do NOT click it.
# * Leaving the editor unsaved raises Chrome's native "Leave site?" dialog in an
#   everyday browser; the driver's take just closes its own Chrome, which drops
#   the change (verified: saved instructions unchanged after three takes).
#
# ---- before the walk ---------------------------------------------------------
# * RUN THIS AGAINST A TEST ORGANIZATION and a TEST unified agent. "I like it"
#   writes the enhanced text into the agent's Instructions field. Do NOT save or
#   publish in the take; discard the change afterwards (see the last note).
# * Account: the admin session in profile/ (target salesmessage). One user, so
#   one take — no second profile needed.
# * The agent: a unified agent whose instructions are deliberately thin, so
#   Enhance has something to add and returns 2-3 recommendations. Keep its id out
#   of this file: put it in .env (e.g. SALESMSG_DEMO_AGENT_ID) as a target secret
#   and open its page with `open /.../{agentId}/...` if a direct URL exists.
# * Enhance calls a model: every wait for "the enhanced version is ready" takes a
#   different, unknowable time. Time it on the walk (waitGone on the loading
#   state, not on a button that might vanish), give it more narration lines than
#   will fit, and let AUTO_SPEED fast-forward whatever narration does not cover.
# * Rules from earlier videos that apply here:
#   - a line is spoken only once what it describes is ON SCREEN: after the modal
#     opens, after the enhanced text is in, after the field is filled;
#   - the holds after a line must cover the line on their own;
#   - prefer btn:Exact Text for chips and buttons; ::-p-text is case-sensitive
#     and can match a hidden copy of the text;
#   - check the starting state (the instructions must be the thin version) so a
#     take that starts from an already-enhanced agent fails fast.

name: enhance-agent-instructions
description: tell Enhance what to improve, review the recommendations, refine, and accept
target: salesmessage
intro: Enhance agent instructions | Choose what to improve, then review before you accept
outro: Thanks for watching | Questions? Reach out any time - we are happy to help

Steps:

# -- open the agent --
Open the test agent's editor directly (/chatbot/{agentId}/config)
Confirm the agent's current Instructions are on screen (the thin starting version)

# -- step 1: say what to improve --
Click Enhance
Confirm the modal opens on step 1 and NOTHING is generating yet — the model is not called until you ask
Confirm the chip group "What to improve?" with Age restriction, Competitor mentions and Clearer goal
Click Age restriction
Click Competitor mentions
Click Clearer goal
Type "Add a rule for complaints" into the custom note (keep notes short: typing in the modal runs ~0.25s a character)
Click Enhance

# -- the result --
Wait for the enhanced version to be ready
Confirm the result view: current instructions on the left, enhanced instructions on the right
Confirm Recommendations pinned above the enhanced text, if any: at most 3 short, single-line, actionable items (sometimes none — do not narrate them unconditionally)
Confirm the enhanced instructions now contain an age verification constraint, a competitor deflection rule, a clear goal for the agent, and a rule for handling complaints
Pause on the enhanced instructions, scrolling to each addition as it is named

# -- refine --
Click Refine
Confirm the modal is back on step 1, now titled "Refine", with the earlier choices and note still in place
Deselect Competitor mentions
Change the custom note to "Add a rule for refunds"
Click Enhance
Wait for the new enhanced version to be ready
Confirm the new enhanced instructions keep the age check and goal, add the refund rule, and drop the competitor and complaint rules

# -- accept --
Click I like it
Confirm the modal closes and the enhanced instructions are now in the Instructions field
Pause on the Instructions field — do NOT click Save or Publish

# ---- after the take (off camera, not part of the video) ----------------------
# Discard the change: close the tab without saving and click Leave on Chrome's
# "Leave site?" dialog, so the next take starts from the same state.
# Not covered here (separate flow if wanted): the calling agent's pre-publish
# validation modal — "Skip for now" / "Edit instructions".
